#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "How a Rose Cross sigil is drawn"
msgstr "How a Rose Cross sigil is drawn"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "The Golden Dawn drew the sigil of a name by tracing it through the letters of the Rose Cross. The rose at its centre carries the 22 letters of the Hebrew alphabet on three rings of petals: the three mother letters innermost, the seven double letters around them and the twelve single letters outside. Israel Regardie printed the Order's rules in <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (1940), with the sigils of Metatron, Elohim and the divine names of Binah drawn as examples. This generator follows those rules."
msgstr "The Golden Dawn drew the sigil of a name by tracing it through the letters of the Rose Cross. The rose at its centre carries the 22 letters of the Hebrew alphabet on three rings of petals: the three mother letters innermost, the seven double letters around them and the twelve single letters outside. Israel Regardie printed the Order's rules in <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (1940), with the sigils of Metatron, Elohim and the divine names of Binah drawn as examples. This generator follows those rules."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "The rules"
msgstr "The rules"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A small circle marks the first letter."
msgstr "A small circle marks the first letter."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A straight line runs from each letter to the next, in order, to the end of the word. Each word of a name is a sigil of its own; this page draws them side by side, right to left."
msgstr "A straight line runs from each letter to the next, in order, to the end of the word. Each word of a name is a sigil of its own; this page draws them side by side, right to left."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Where a letter is doubled, as in the two Teths of Metatron, the line makes a crook or wave at that letter: one wave for each repeat, so a letter written three times has two."
msgstr "Where a letter is doubled, as in the two Teths of Metatron, the line makes a crook or wave at that letter: one wave for each repeat, so a letter written three times has two."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Where the line passes straight through a letter of the name, as Metatron's runs through Resh, a small loop beside the line marks the letter, so that the stop can be seen."
msgstr "Where the line passes straight through a letter of the name, as Metatron's runs through Resh, a small loop beside the line marks the letter, so that the stop can be seen."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A short bar across the line ends the sigil at the last letter."
msgstr "A short bar across the line ends the sigil at the last letter."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A final letter is traced at the place of its ordinary form, and anything else, such as vowel points, is left out."
msgstr "A final letter is traced at the place of its ordinary form, and anything else, such as vowel points, is left out."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "What Regardie's figures show"
msgstr "What Regardie's figures show"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "The text leaves some cases open, and the worked sigils settle them:"
msgstr "The text leaves some cases open, and the worked sigils settle them:"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A line that returns to a letter it has already visited, as YHVH returns to He, is drawn just beside the first visit, so the two strokes stay apart."
msgstr "A line that returns to a letter it has already visited, as YHVH returns to He, is drawn just beside the first visit, so the two strokes stay apart."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A line that crosses a letter which is not in the name gets no mark."
msgstr "A line that crosses a letter which is not in the name gets no mark."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "A line that crosses a letter of the name on its way somewhere else gets no loop either: only a letter the line passes through between its own neighbours does."
msgstr "A line that crosses a letter of the name on its way somewhere else gets no loop either: only a letter the line passes through between its own neighbours does."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Lines cross the centre of the rose, and each other, freely."
msgstr "Lines cross the centre of the rose, and each other, freely."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "How this generator draws them"
msgstr "How this generator draws them"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Regardie does not say how nearly straight a line must run to count as passing through a letter. The generator draws a loop only where the letter lies within one unit of the straight line between its neighbours, on a rose a hundred units across; any line bent more than that turns a visible corner instead."
msgstr "Regardie does not say how nearly straight a line must run to count as passing through a letter. The generator draws a loop only where the letter lies within one unit of the straight line between its neighbours, on a rose a hundred units across; any line bent more than that turns a visible corner instead."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Each letter's point is placed by these rules rather than adjusted by a numerical optimiser, so a name always gives the same sigil: on this page, in a downloaded image and in a shared link. Where a return or a mark would touch another line, the point moves within its letter's place until every mark stands clear. A long word can crowd the rose so that no such placement exists, and the page then says so."
msgstr "Each letter's point is placed by these rules rather than adjusted by a numerical optimiser, so a name always gives the same sigil: on this page, in a downloaded image and in a shared link. Where a return or a mark would touch another line, the point moves within its letter's place until every mark stands clear. A long word can crowd the rose so that no such placement exists, and the page then says so."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "The rose has two arrangements of the double letters. The Golden Dawn's, as The Equinox printed it in 1910, is the default; Regardie's edition of 1939 exchanges Kaph and Tau. Regardie's own sigils in volume 4 are drawn on the Golden Dawn's arrangement."
msgstr "The rose has two arrangements of the double letters. The Golden Dawn's, as The Equinox printed it in 1910, is the default; Regardie's edition of 1939 exchanges Kaph and Tau. Regardie's own sigils in volume 4 are drawn on the Golden Dawn's arrangement."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Try <0>Metatron</0>, <1>Elohim</1>, <2>YHVH Elohim</2> or <3>Shabbathai</3>, or the names of the <4>72 angels</4>, such as <5>Vehuiah</5>."
msgstr "Try <0>Metatron</0>, <1>Elohim</1>, <2>YHVH Elohim</2> or <3>Shabbathai</3>, or the names of the <4>72 angels</4>, such as <5>Vehuiah</5>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Every one of the <0>72 angels' pages</0> shows the sigil of its name, with the files to download, as <1>Vehuiah's</1> does."
msgstr "Every one of the <0>72 angels' pages</0> shows the sigil of its name, with the files to download, as <1>Vehuiah's</1> does."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Regardie also sets out a way of tracing names on the planets' magic squares: the <0>kamea sigil generator</0> draws a name's sigil on the kamea of its planet."
msgstr "Regardie also sets out a way of tracing names on the planets' magic squares: the <0>kamea sigil generator</0> draws a name's sigil on the kamea of its planet."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Sources"
msgstr "Sources"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "Israel Regardie, <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (Aries Press, Chicago, 1940): the rules on <1>page 57</1>; Metatron and Elohim on <2>page 58</2>; the sigils of the names of Binah on <3>pages 59</3> and <4>60</4>. The scans are on archive.org. The book is in the public domain in the United States but still in copyright elsewhere, so its pages are linked rather than shown here."
msgstr "Israel Regardie, <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (Aries Press, Chicago, 1940): the rules on <1>page 57</1>; Metatron and Elohim on <2>page 58</2>; the sigils of the names of Binah on <3>pages 59</3> and <4>60</4>. The scans are on archive.org. The book is in the public domain in the United States but still in copyright elsewhere, so its pages are linked rather than shown here."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/gd/sigils/SigilsText.tsx
msgid "The rules, the figures' evidence and how the generator is tested against them, every pair and triple of letters included, are set out in <0>the project's design notes</0>."
msgstr "The rules, the figures' evidence and how the generator is tested against them, every pair and triple of letters included, are set out in <0>the project's design notes</0>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
