#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksPage.tsx
msgid "Public-domain works of the Western esoteric tradition, read from their original scans and published in full, with an editorial apparatus recording every place the reading departs from the page."
msgstr "Public-domain works of the Western esoteric tradition, read from their original scans and published in full, with an editorial apparatus recording every place the reading departs from the page."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksPage.tsx
msgid "<0>La Science Cabalistique</0> — Lazare Lenain, Amiens, 1823. The 72 angels of the Kabbalah, their attributes, seals and hours."
msgstr "<0>La Science Cabalistique</0> — Lazare Lenain, Amiens, 1823. The 72 angels of the Kabbalah, their attributes, seals and hours."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksText.tsx
msgid "About these editions"
msgstr "About these editions"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksText.tsx
msgid "Each book is read page by page from a scan of the printed book, not from machine OCR. Where the original is wrong, a misprinted date, a misnumbered entry or a miscounted total, the text keeps the author's words and a note says what is wrong and what it should be. Every page marker links to the facsimile of its leaf. You can always check the reading against the page it was made from."
msgstr "Each book is read page by page from a scan of the printed book, not from machine OCR. Where the original is wrong, a misprinted date, a misnumbered entry or a miscounted total, the text keeps the author's words and a note says what is wrong and what it should be. Every page marker links to the facsimile of its leaf. You can always check the reading against the page it was made from."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksText.tsx
msgid "<0>La Science Cabalistique</0>, Lazare Lenain's book of 1823, was the first work in French on the 72 angels of the Kabbalah. It was printed in 500 copies and sold by the author from his reading room. It sets out the 72 genii of the Shem HaMephorash and the arithmetic of Lenain's four cabalistic tables. Each genius takes five degrees of the zodiac, five days of the year and twenty minutes of each day."
msgstr "<0>La Science Cabalistique</0>, Lazare Lenain's book of 1823, was the first work in French on the 72 angels of the Kabbalah. It was printed in 500 copies and sold by the author from his reading room. It sets out the 72 genii of the Shem HaMephorash and the arithmetic of Lenain's four cabalistic tables. Each genius takes five degrees of the zodiac, five days of the year and twenty minutes of each day."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksText.tsx
msgid "The edition is in French, chapter by chapter, from a later reissue with a preface by Papus. For the angels in English, see <0>the 72 angels</0>. Their names, dates and correspondences are translated from Lenain's French alone, and each angel has its own page, from <1>Vehuiah</1> to <2>Mumiah</2>. The <3>Shem HaMephorash</3> page explains the name they come from."
msgstr "The edition is in French, chapter by chapter, from a later reissue with a preface by Papus. For the angels in English, see <0>the 72 angels</0>. Their names, dates and correspondences are translated from Lenain's French alone, and each angel has its own page, from <1>Vehuiah</1> to <2>Mumiah</2>. The <3>Shem HaMephorash</3> page explains the name they come from."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/books/BooksText.tsx
msgid "Lenain died in 1877 and Papus in 1916, so both texts are in the public domain. This reading of them is CC BY 4.0."
msgstr "Lenain died in 1877 and Papus in 1916, so both texts are in the public domain. This reading of them is CC BY 4.0."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "In Agrippa's square the number in row 1, column 2 is damaged in the print; his Hebrew table beside it has 24, which the square needs."
msgstr "In Agrippa's square the number in row 1, column 2 is damaged in the print; his Hebrew table beside it has 24, which the square needs."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa's square prints 45 in row 4, column 5, where his Hebrew table has 43, which the square needs; the square here has 43."
msgstr "Agrippa's square prints 45 in row 4, column 5, where his Hebrew table has 43, which the square needs; the square here has 43."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Regardie's volume 4 prints 43 in row 2, column 3, where Agrippa has 48, so that 43 stands in the square twice."
msgstr "Regardie's volume 4 prints 43 in row 2, column 3, where Agrippa has 48, so that 43 stands in the square twice."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa's Hebrew table leaves the cell of 10 blank."
msgstr "Agrippa's Hebrew table leaves the cell of 10 blank."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Regardie's volume 4 swaps three pairs of numbers: 45 and 48 in row 3, and 35 and 38, and 25 and 28, in row 4. Its rows still add up to 260; its columns do not. None of the swapped cells is one that Taphthartharath's sigil passes through."
msgstr "Regardie's volume 4 swaps three pairs of numbers: 45 and 48 in row 3, and 35 and 38, and 25 and 28, in row 4. Its rows still add up to 260; its columns do not. None of the swapped cells is one that Taphthartharath's sigil passes through."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa prints 45 in row 1, column 8, in both his tables, where the square needs 54; the square here has 54."
msgstr "Agrippa prints 45 in row 1, column 8, in both his tables, where the square needs 54; the square here has 54."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Regardie's volume 4 prints 54 there, as the square needs."
msgstr "Regardie's volume 4 prints 54 there, as the square needs."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "A magic square of {order} by {order}: the numbers 1 to {cells}, set so that every row, every column and both diagonals add up to {line}, and all of them together to {total}."
msgstr "A magic square of {order} by {order}: the numbers 1 to {cells}, set so that every row, every column and both diagonals add up to {line}, and all of them together to {total}."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa's square is the one this rule makes: 1 goes in the cell just below the centre, and each next number one cell down and one to the right, wrapping round at the edges, or two cells down where that cell is taken."
msgstr "Agrippa's square is the one this rule makes: 1 goes in the cell just below the centre, and each next number one cell down and one to the right, wrapping round at the edges, or two cells down where that cell is taken."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa's square is the one this rule makes: write the numbers 1 to {cells} in order, row by row; exchange every number on a diagonal of each four-by-four block for {complement} less that number; then read the rows from the bottom up."
msgstr "Agrippa's square is the one this rule makes: write the numbers 1 to {cells} in order, row by row; exchange every number on a diagonal of each four-by-four block for {complement} less that number; then read the rows from the bottom up."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "No rule as simple as the odd squares' or those of four and eight makes a square of six, and the square here is Agrippa's as he prints it."
msgstr "No rule as simple as the odd squares' or those of four and eight makes a square of six, and the square here is Agrippa's as he prints it."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its intelligence and its spirit. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."
msgstr "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its intelligence and its spirit. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its intelligence, its spirit and its intelligences, the Bne Seraphim. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."
msgstr "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its intelligence, its spirit and its intelligences, the Bne Seraphim. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its spirit, its spirit of spirits and its intelligence of intelligences. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."
msgstr "Agrippa prints the square in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22, on <1>page {page}</1>, in numbers and again in Hebrew letters, with the planet's seal and the characters of its spirit, its spirit of spirits and its intelligence of intelligences. Regardie's plates in <2>The Golden Dawn</2>, volume 4 (1940), draw it again, on <3>page {regardiePage}</3>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "The square here is Agrippa's as the 1533 printing gives it."
msgstr "The square here is Agrippa's as the 1533 printing gives it."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "The square here is Agrippa's with the slip of the 1533 printing noted below corrected; whether it is the author's or the printer's, the evidence read does not settle."
msgstr "The square here is Agrippa's with the slip of the 1533 printing noted below corrected; whether it is the author's or the printer's, the evidence read does not settle."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "Agrippa gives the Moon no single intelligence. In its place he names an intelligence of intelligences, and beside its spirit a spirit of spirits, both numbered 3321, the sum of the square, which their letters reach only with the final letters counted at 500 to 900. Shelachel, the Moon's intelligence in present-day sources, comes last."
msgstr "Agrippa gives the Moon no single intelligence. In its place he names an intelligence of intelligences, and beside its spirit a spirit of spirits, both numbered 3321, the sum of the square, which their letters reach only with the final letters counted at 500 to 900. Shelachel, the Moon's intelligence in present-day sources, comes last."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/kameaCopy.ts
msgid "On the Moon's square the tens from 10 to 80 stand in one column, the fourth, with 9 among them. The method Regardie sets out keeps a letter's number where the square has it and takes a larger one down to its tens or units, so every letter from Yod to Tav falls in that column: Yod to Peh keep their tens, Tzadi's 90 becomes 9, and Qof to Tav become 10 to 40. A long name's sigil on this square runs up and down that one column, and its marks are hard to set clear of each other, as the <0>generator</0> shows. This is the method's doing, not a fault of the square."
msgstr "On the Moon's square the tens from 10 to 80 stand in one column, the fourth, with 9 among them. The method Regardie sets out keeps a letter's number where the square has it and takes a larger one down to its tens or units, so every letter from Yod to Tav falls in that column: Yod to Peh keep their tens, Tzadi's 90 becomes 9, and Qof to Tav become 10 to 40. A long name's sigil on this square runs up and down that one column, and its marks are hard to set clear of each other, as the <0>generator</0> shows. This is the method's doing, not a fault of the square."

