msgstr "Drawn from the strokes recorded by {reader}, one of the two readers: straight between the points it read, curved where it read a curve. A ring is a circle it read at an end or on a line; a bar or a hook is drawn where it placed one; a dashed ring is an end mark it did not name. The woodcut's line weight and rounded turns are not drawn."

