msgstr "Regardie's plates in <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (1940), draw the character again, on <1>page {page}</1>. That book is in copyright where this site is read, so his figure is neither shown nor redrawn here; this is our reading of it."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/NamePage.tsx
msgid "How this was read: each figure was cropped from the scan and given a number in place of its name. Two readers, Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.2, working apart, recorded its strokes, the points along them and the marks at their ends. Two judges, the same two models working apart, then compared each figure and both readings with the trace of every witness's spelling. Where the judges agreed, their verdict stands; where they differed, on 7 of the 32 figures, Claude Opus 5.5 weighed both judges' reasons against the figure and settled it, and the note with the verdict says how. The readings and verdicts are in the <0>table of Agrippa's characters</0>."
msgstr "How this was read: each figure was cropped from the scan and given a number in place of its name. Two readers, Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.2, working apart, recorded its strokes, the points along them and the marks at their ends. Two judges, the same two models working apart, then compared each figure and both readings with the trace of every witness's spelling. Where the judges agreed, their verdict stands; where they differed, on 7 of the 32 figures, Claude Opus 5.5 weighed both judges' reasons against the figure and settled it, and the note with the verdict says how. The readings and verdicts are in the <0>table of Agrippa's characters</0>."

