msgstr "This sigil could not be drawn."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "How a kamea sigil is drawn"
msgstr "How a kamea sigil is drawn"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "A kamea is a planet's magic square: the numbers from one up to the square of its order, set so that every row, column and diagonal adds up to the same sum. Agrippa printed the seven in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (1533), from Saturn's three by three to the Moon's nine by nine, with the names of each planet's intelligence and spirit, whose letters add up to the square's numbers. Israel Regardie, in <1>The Golden Dawn</1> (volume 4, 1940), sets out a method of tracing those names on the squares to draw their sigils, which he writes the Order had lost by his day (<2>page 78</2>), and this generator traces any Hebrew name by it."
msgstr "A kamea is a planet's magic square: the numbers from one up to the square of its order, set so that every row, column and diagonal adds up to the same sum. Agrippa printed the seven in <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (1533), from Saturn's three by three to the Moon's nine by nine, with the names of each planet's intelligence and spirit, whose letters add up to the square's numbers. Israel Regardie, in <1>The Golden Dawn</1> (volume 4, 1940), sets out a method of tracing those names on the squares to draw their sigils, which he writes the Order had lost by his day (<2>page 78</2>), and this generator traces any Hebrew name by it."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "The method"
msgstr "The method"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Each letter is counted at its number: Aleph 1 to Tet 9, Yod 10 to Tzadi 90, Qof 100 to Tav 400."
msgstr "Each letter is counted at its number: Aleph 1 to Tet 9, Yod 10 to Tzadi 90, Qof 100 to Tav 400."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "A number the square has is kept. A larger one is reduced by Aiq Bekar, the Qabalah of nine chambers, to its tens or its units: divided by ten until the square has it. On Saturn's square Zazel keeps 7, 1 and 7 and takes Lamed's 30 as 3; on Mercury's, Taphthartharath takes Tav's 400 as 40."
msgstr "A number the square has is kept. A larger one is reduced by Aiq Bekar, the Qabalah of nine chambers, to its tens or its units: divided by ten until the square has it. On Saturn's square Zazel keeps 7, 1 and 7 and takes Lamed's 30 as 3; on Mercury's, Taphthartharath takes Tav's 400 as 40."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "A line runs through the cells in the order of the letters, from a small circle at the first to a short bar at the last."
msgstr "A line runs through the cells in the order of the letters, from a small circle at the first to a short bar at the last."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Where two letters in a row fall on one cell, the line makes a crook there; where it passes straight through a cell of the name, a small loop marks the stop; and a line that comes back to a cell it has visited is drawn just beside the first visit, as on the <0>Rose Cross sigils</0>."
msgstr "Where two letters in a row fall on one cell, the line makes a crook there; where it passes straight through a cell of the name, a small loop marks the stop; and a line that comes back to a cell it has visited is drawn just beside the first visit, as on the <0>Rose Cross sigils</0>."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "The table under the sigil shows each letter, its number and the cell it falls on."
msgstr "The table under the sigil shows each letter, its number and the cell it falls on."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "What the generator chooses"
msgstr "What the generator chooses"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Final letters. Aiq Bekar puts the five final forms in the hundreds from 500 to 900, but neither of Regardie's worked examples has one. A final letter counts at its ordinary letter's number unless you choose the table's values, which some of Agrippa's printed sums need."
msgstr "Final letters. Aiq Bekar puts the five final forms in the hundreds from 500 to 900, but neither of Regardie's worked examples has one. A final letter counts at its ordinary letter's number unless you choose the table's values, which some of Agrippa's printed sums need."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Words. Each word of a name is its own figure on its own square, set right to left, as the Rose Cross sigils are."
msgstr "Words. Each word of a name is its own figure on its own square, set right to left, as the Rose Cross sigils are."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "The marks. The crook, the loop and the end bar are the Rose Cross sigil's, at a size fixed against the square. Agrippa's own characters put a circle at both ends of most figures, and Regardie's plates mostly a circle at the start and a bar or nothing at the end."
msgstr "The marks. The crook, the loop and the end bar are the Rose Cross sigil's, at a size fixed against the square. Agrippa's own characters put a circle at both ends of most figures, and Regardie's plates mostly a circle at the start and a bar or nothing at the end."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "The Moon's square. On it 10 to 80 stand in one column, so nearly every letter from Yod on falls there, and a long name runs up and down that column. A name whose marks cannot all be set clear of each other and of the square's lines is drawn as well as it can be, and the page says so."
msgstr "The Moon's square. On it 10 to 80 stand in one column, so nearly every letter from Yod on falls there, and a long name runs up and down that column. A name whose marks cannot all be set clear of each other and of the square's lines is drawn as well as it can be, and the page says so."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Agrippa prints the Moon's spirit of spirits as one word of fourteen letters. The list gives it so, and first divided as its romanisation divides it, Schedbarschemoth Schartathan, which is how this site traces it; that division is ours, not Agrippa's."
msgstr "Agrippa prints the Moon's spirit of spirits as one word of fourteen letters. The list gives it so, and first divided as its romanisation divides it, Schedbarschemoth Schartathan, which is how this site traces it; that division is ours, not Agrippa's."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Agrippa's printed characters are largely traces of the names on the squares, drawn freely, but not every one follows this reduction, so the sigils here are not presented as his. Try <0>Agiel</0> on Saturn's square, <1>Taphthartharath</1> on Mercury's or <2>Chasmodai</2> on the Moon's, or choose a name from the list for each planet, which gives every witness's spelling where they differ."
msgstr "Agrippa's printed characters are largely traces of the names on the squares, drawn freely, but not every one follows this reduction, so the sigils here are not presented as his. Try <0>Agiel</0> on Saturn's square, <1>Taphthartharath</1> on Mercury's or <2>Chasmodai</2> on the Moon's, or choose a name from the list for each planet, which gives every witness's spelling where they differ."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa, <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22: the names and their numbers on <1>leaf 163</1>, the Moon's with the squares of Saturn and Jupiter on <2>leaf 164</2>, and the Moon's square on <3>leaf 168</3>, from the Library of Congress copy on archive.org."
msgstr "Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa, <0>De occulta philosophia</0> (Cologne, 1533), book II, chapter 22: the names and their numbers on <1>leaf 163</1>, the Moon's with the squares of Saturn and Jupiter on <2>leaf 164</2>, and the Moon's square on <3>leaf 168</3>, from the Library of Congress copy on archive.org."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "Israel Regardie, <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (Aries Press, Chicago, 1940): the method on <1>pages 78</1> to <2>80</2>, with the Aiq Bekar table on <3>page 79</3>. The book is in the public domain in the United States but still in copyright elsewhere, so its pages are linked rather than shown here."
msgstr "Israel Regardie, <0>The Golden Dawn</0>, volume 4 (Aries Press, Chicago, 1940): the method on <1>pages 78</1> to <2>80</2>, with the Aiq Bekar table on <3>page 79</3>. The book is in the public domain in the United States but still in copyright elsewhere, so its pages are linked rather than shown here."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/app/astrology/kamea/sigils/KameaSigilsText.tsx
msgid "The names by witness, where the printings disagree, and how the generator is tested on every name and every triple of letters on each square, are set out in <0>the project's design notes</0>."
msgstr "The names by witness, where the printings disagree, and how the generator is tested on every name and every triple of letters on each square, are set out in <0>the project's design notes</0>."

